  "id": "u09-l03",
  "unit": "u09-past",
  "title": "Went, came, ate",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "A handful of everyday verbs have irregular pasts. Learn them as words:\n\n- যাওয়া 'go' → **গেলাম** 'I went', **গেল** 'he/she went'\n- আসা 'come' → **এলাম** 'I came' (Bangladesh also: **আসলাম**)\n- খাওয়া 'eat / drink' → **খেলাম** 'I ate'\n- দেওয়া 'give' → **দিলাম** 'I gave'\n- নেওয়া 'take' → **নিলাম** 'I took'\n\nThe endings are still regular: -লাম, -লে, -ল… only the stem changes.\n\n**এলাম vs আসলাম:** both are heard across Bangladesh. **এলাম** is the standard (and Kolkata) form; **আসলাম** is very common in relaxed Bangladeshi speech. Understand both, use either.",
  "vocab": [
